[2026-05-07T14:11:03.298Z] [INFO] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_125","type":"reasoning","text":"**Analyzing code changes**\n\nI'm looking at the origin/main test 2414 and checking why there are four additions. In the current file after the merge, I noticed that test-2414 includes what looks like duplicate color helper extracts. This could stem from an earlier auto-merge related to issue 2426. \n\nThe diff shows these duplicates after certain functions, which is strange since the tests seem to pass. I wonder if we should remove one of the duplicates to keep things clean; let’s review current versus origin/main to make a decision.\n**Inspecting test-2414 code**\n\nIn test-2414, I see some code snippets like `${dashAttr}`, `${dashBrowserSupportsColor}`, and others listed, but there's a duplicate present. It seems this may have resulted from an automatic merge, which isn’t necessary here.\n\nWhile it's part of the PR diff, it looks like issue 2428 might not be related. I think we should remove the first duplicate set to keep the PR diff smaller and ensure it matches origin/main more effectively.\n**Reviewing commit changes**\n\nI need to add a small commit, but it seems there’s a duplicate part of a merge commit; I can make a follow-up commit to address that. I’ll need to push the changes after removing the first duplicate block in `experiments/test-issue-2414...` following dashAttr. I may also need to update the PR body regarding tests and possibly add issue 2430 later. It's worth checking for any unintended diffs since `git diff origin/main` shows 17 files and I was only expecting those from issue 2428. Let's go ahead and patch this!"}}
